# Corpus unit pinn/C03 — gap (a spectral comparison whose estimator error is unquantified)
#
# Source: m0/annotations/pinn.yaml C03 (causal, component_spectral_comparison; corpus pin
# 62e9b54). Headline: the residual loss component (the differential-operator term) is the
# dominant source of ill-conditioning — for each PDE in {convection, reaction, wave} the
# residual-component Hessian's max eigenvalue exceeds the IC and BC components', which are
# comparatively well-conditioned, and theory predicts the operator D is the source (E02,
# Figure 3/7; Theorem 8.4 via C07/E05).
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * component_spectral_comparison maps to the controlled_comparison family: conclusion
#     better(residual_component, ic_bc_components, ill_conditioning, pinn_pdes) — the residual
#     component "wins" on the ill-conditioning (max-eigenvalue) axis. IC and BC are folded into
#     one comparand constant; per-PDE cells and the two well-conditioned components stay in nl
#     and refs.
#   * The mandatory measurement_validity CQ is unmet-gap: E02 names SLQ (PyHessian or
#     equivalent) but Metrics report only the visual spectra with no estimator error bars, so
#     the cross-component max-eigenvalue ordering is untrusted. variance_reported is also unmet
#     (a single best Adam+L-BFGS checkpoint per PDE, no seeds/widths/stages). Open mandatory
#     obligations make the argument an IncompleteArgument rejection, so no complete
#     controlled_comparison is declarable — E2-style gap on empty complete support
#     (adaptive-pruning/C03 pattern). baseline_parity (all three spectra from the same
#     checkpoint with the same SLQ procedure) is annotated met and kept as a leaf.
#   * Coverage flag (kind-a, summary §3): C03 has two heterogeneous support strands (the E02
#     spectral comparison and the Theorem 8.4 operator-conditioning prediction), but one
#     inference_scheme per claim; the theoretical strand (annotated met, met via E05/C07) is
#     folded into a premise/nl note here rather than a second arg, per the no-accrual decision.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact pinn at sha256:116d458ce7eb
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, not assemblable at corpus-v1's evidential bar --------------------------

claim c03
  nl      = "The residual loss component (the differential-operator term) is the dominant source of ill-conditioning: for convection, reaction, and wave the residual-component Hessian max eigenvalue exceeds the comparatively well-conditioned IC and BC components, and theory predicts the operator D is the source"
  formal  = better(residual_component, ic_bc_components, ill_conditioning, pinn_pdes)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = reviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves are present ... ------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: E02's per-PDE cross-component max-eigenvalue ordering, per result cell,
# folded into refs; the theoretical strand (Theorem 8.4 via C07/E05) is noted in nl.
leaf e1 : reports(e02, compares(residual_component, ic_bc_components, ill_conditioning, pinn_pdes, favorable))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [Figure-3-bottom, Figure-7, section-5.2, Theorem-8.4, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N05]

leaf e2 : matched_setup(residual_component, ic_bc_components, e02)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E02-Procedure-step-1, logic/experiments.md#E02-Procedure-step-3, logic/experiments.md#E02-Procedure-step-6]

# --- ... but no complete argument is declarable -------------------------------------------------

# (Intentionally no `arg`: valid_measurement(ill_conditioning, e02) has no honest leaf — SLQ
# estimator error is unquantified, so the component ordering rests on visual spectra — and
# variance_reported is likewise unmet (one best checkpoint per PDE). Both are mandatory in
# corpus-v1. The claim's complete-support set is therefore empty.)

status c03

# ==============================================================================================
